-- chem/linkhop.hypercubical — the electron on one link, from chem/bholonomy.hypercubical's hop and nothing else.
-- Two four-valent vertices v and w joined by a link of doubled spin x; at each, the neighbouring link coupled first
-- has spin ½ (v2 = w2 = 1), v's outer label is kt = 0 and w's is m = 1. The electron at v forces k = 1, so the
-- link is x = 0 or x = 2; the electron at w leaves the link at x2 = 1 with w's inner label m2 = 0 or 2. The hop
-- is then a 2 × 2 matrix B between (x = 0, x = 2) and (m2 = 0, m2 = 2) with entries `hop-amp`, each a sign and the
-- square root of a rational. Checked: both columns have norm one, the columns are orthogonal, and the rows have
-- norm one, so B is orthogonal; its entries at m2 = 0 are −1/2 and +√3/2 (squares 64/256 and 1728/2304).
-- Consequence, a statement here: the hop on this pair of vertices is [[0, B], [Bᵀ, 0]], whose square is 1, so the
-- electron on one link has exactly the two levels ±1 in units of the hop amplitude, with no dependence on which
-- of the link's spins it started from.
-- A leaf: no module imports it.
import "bholonomy.hypercubical"

